## Introduction

For my final project in STAT 301-1, I want to look at heart disease deaths in
the U.S. My main question is: how do heart disease death rates change across
counties, and how do they differ by sex and race/ethnicity? I picked this
topic because heart disease is a big public health problem and I want to see
where and in which groups it is most common.

## Data Source

I am using the CDC's *Heart Disease Mortality Data Among US Adults (35+) by
State/Territory and County, 2022–2024*. It is on the
[CDC Data Portal](https://data.cdc.gov/d/mri7-5jtw). The rates are averaged
over three years, so I can't use this data to look at changes over time.

## Data Import

```{r}
library(tidyverse)

heart_data <- read_csv(
  "https://data.cdc.gov/api/views/mri7-5jtw/rows.csv?accessType=DOWNLOAD"
)
```

